🚨 Real-time Terraform challenge today! 🚨
While running terraform apply on my environment, I hit this annoying error:

Error: EntityAlreadyExists: Role "devops-role" already exists.

😅 What happened:

 I was re-deploying infrastructure, but AWS already had some resources created manually. 

Terraform, expecting a fresh start, couldn’t create the IAM role and failed. A classic “Terraform vs Reality” moment!

💡 How I solved it:
 1️⃣ Checked the existing resources in AWS.
 2️⃣ Synced Terraform state with existing resources using:

terraform import aws_iam_role.devops_role devops-role

3️⃣ Ran terraform plan → then terraform apply successfully ✅

🔥 Lesson learned:

* Terraform is powerful, but it needs to know the current state.
* Manual changes in the cloud can create unexpected errors.
* Always import existing resources before applying changes.

💭 Takeaway: DevOps isn’t just code—it’s understanding the reality of your infrastructure. Every error teaches something!
